    "created_at": "2017-05-22T18:25:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-22T18:25:10Z",
    "body": "I was only planning to block `http` and `https` URLs. If it turns out that we can block unencoded `<` in `data:` as well, I wouldn't have a problem doing so. If Firefox and IE don't support that syntax, perhaps we can get away with it?\r\n\r\nI'll look at the data again on that point in particular tomorrow.",
