    "body": "The `.utf8` isn't necessary, as even malformed charset expressions work (since the URI is already in a known encoding, usually). \r\n\r\nGood to see browsers converged, though. I think even Chrome/WebKit still barf on non-ASCII octets in Unicode, but that's no longer under this issue's scope.",
